        "g_serves": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "users",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Serves 4",
            "text": "<p>One 16 oz bag of shrimp, four 4 oz servings, over cilantro lime basmati. It halves cleanly if you are cooking for two and want leftovers of the sauce.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_prep": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Watch for the C",
            "text": "<p>Shrimp are done when they curl into a loose C. A closed O means overcooked, and a thick sauce keeps cooking them after the heat is off.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
