        "m_head": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The sauce is the make-ahead",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "m_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Everything up to the shrimp keeps. Roast the pumpkin, blend the sauce and bloom the spices, then refrigerate the finished sauce for up to three days &mdash; it thickens as it sits, so loosen it with a splash of water or coconut milk when you reheat. The toasted coconut and pepitas keep for a fortnight in a jar at room temperature.</p><p>Cook the shrimp fresh. They take four minutes, they are the one thing that cannot be reheated without going rubbery, and they are the reason to make this rather than a vegetable curry.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "m_btn": {
